Drive any Payload CMS 3.x project through its REST API.

PayCLI is built for LLM coding agents: every command prints one JSON envelope
with a stable shape, a machine-readable error code and an exit code that maps to
a class of failure. Run `pay explain` first — it answers "what can I do here?"
in a single call, offline after the first discovery.

SYNOPSIS
  pay [flags]

  Subcommands:
    access         Show what this credential is permitted to do (GET /api/access).
    audit          Inspect the local write-audit log
    auth           Manage profiles and credentials (§5).
    cache          Inspect and manage the discovery cache
    can            Answer one permission question with an exit code (0 permitted, 8 denied).
    collections    List this project's collections with their ops, features and key fields.
    completion     Print a shell completion script for pay.
    config         Inspect and edit PayCLI's own configuration (§4).
    count          Count the documents matching a filter (GET /api/{collection}/count)
    create         Create one document (POST /api/{collection})
    delete         Delete one document by id, or every document matching --where
    describe       Print one entity's full field schema: types, operators, required, relations.
    discover       Probe this Payload project and cache its schema (§7 discovery pipeline).
    doctor         Diagnose this project, this profile and this machine in one JSON document.
    download       Download the bytes of an upload document
    duplicate      Copy one document
    explain        Answer "what can I do here?" in one call — cache-backed and offline after the first run.
    find           List documents in a collection (GET /api/{collection})
    get            Fetch one document by id (GET /api/{collection}/{id})
    globals        Read and write Payload globals
    publish        Set _status=published on one document or every match
    raw            Call any Payload endpoint PayCLI does not model
    restore        Un-trash a soft-deleted document
    skills         Install the PayCLI agent skill
    unpublish      Set _status=draft on one document or every match
    update         Update one document by id, or every document matching --where (PATCH)
    update-self    Check for and install a newer pay binary
    upload         Upload a file to an upload-enabled collection
    version        Print the PayCLI build stamp (and, with --check, whether a newer release exists).
    versions       Inspect, compare and restore document versions
    whoami         Show the identity this credential resolves to (GET /api/{auth}/me).

FLAGS
    --accept-language ACCEPT-LANGUAGE Accept-Language sent to Payload (default en)
    --api-key API-KEY            API key (prefer --api-key-stdin: argv is world-readable)
    --api-key-file API-KEY-FILE  read the API key from a 0600 file
    --api-key-stdin              read the API key from the first line of stdin
    --api-path API-PATH          Payload routes.api prefix (default /api)
    --auth-collection AUTH-COLLECTION auth collection slug; "auto" discovers it
    --auth-header-scheme AUTH-HEADER-SCHEME JWT|Bearer — the scheme used for a token
    --auth-mode AUTH-MODE        auto|api-key|jwt|anonymous
    --base-url BASE-URL          Payload server origin, e.g. http://localhost:3000
    --cache-ttl CACHE-TTL        override the discovery cache TTL for this run
    --concurrency N              parallel requests (default 8, hard cap 32)
    --config CONFIG              path to config.toml
    --deadline DEADLINE          whole-command deadline (default 120s)
    --dry-run                    print what would be sent and exit 0 without sending it
    --errors-to ERRORS-TO        stdout|stderr — where the error envelope goes
    --fallback-locale FALLBACK-LOCALE CODE|none|default
    --graphql-path GRAPHQL-PATH  full GraphQL path; overrides --api-path + --graphql-route
    --graphql-route GRAPHQL-ROUTE GraphQL route appended to --api-path (default /graphql)
    -h, --help                   help for pay
    --insecure-skip-verify       skip TLS verification (dev only)
    --locale LOCALE              locale for localized fields
    --log-format LOG-FORMAT      text|json
    --log-level LOG-LEVEL        debug|info|warn|error
    --max-retries N              retry budget for idempotent requests (default 3)
    --no-audit                   do not write the audit log for this command
    --no-cache                   ignore and do not write the discovery cache
    --no-color                   accepted for compatibility; PayCLI never colours output
    --no-raw                     omit Payload's raw response body from the envelope
    --no-redact                  do not redact secrets in output (dangerous)
    --output OUTPUT              json|jsonl|table|csv|id|raw (default json, never TTY-dependent)
    --path PATH                  apply a three-form path expression to .data (§10.3; NOT jq)
    --profile PROFILE            named profile to use
    -q, --quiet                  suppress the human stderr summary
    --refresh                    force re-discovery before running
    --timeout TIMEOUT            per-request timeout (default 30s)
    -v, --verbose                log every request at debug level
    --version                    version for pay
    --yes                        assume yes for every confirmation prompt

OUTPUT
  data_kind: op_result
  Envelope: {"ok":true,"v":1,"command":"…","data_kind":"…","data":…,"meta":{…},"warnings":[]}

EXIT CODES
    0   success
    1   internal — a PayCLI bug, a corrupt cache or an unwritable audit log
  
  Full table: pay explain --section exit_codes

EXAMPLES
  (none recorded for this command)

COMMON MISTAKES
  (none recorded for this command)

SEE ALSO
  pay explain    # what can I do here?
  pay doctor     # why is this failing?

